The skeleton of the RLVM journal is ready (journal lead, 2026-11-24).

READ FIRST: journal/AGENTS.md (kinds of trees, frontmatter, "Numbers", "Writing rules",
"What must not be written", "Markup"). The site and the repository are public.

TOOLS (prebuilt; run them with journal/ as the working directory):
  result-tools/bin/journal-new <design|decision|problem|log|example|motivation|insight|session>
      allocates a random address, creates trees/<dir>/<address>.tree with one \date line
      (replace that line with the frontmatter of AGENTS.md; \date is YYYY-MM-DD, the date of the work)
  result-tools/bin/journal-check
      builds a scratch copy of the forest and fails on any diagnostic; it does not write output/,
      so it is safe while others work. It shows the diagnostics of ALL trees: fix those in your
      directories, ignore the others (their owner is mid-edit).
  Do NOT run journal-build, journal-serve, nix build or nix develop in journal/ (they write output/
  or copy the directory); the lead does the site builds.
  scripts/md2tree.py converts a markdown fragment: python3 scripts/md2tree.py draft.md <address>
  (keep drafts outside journal/, for example under work/).

MACROS (\import{base-macros}): \table \tr \th \td, \src{docs/design/ISA.md} (a file of the
repository, path as the argument, no \verb inside), \commit{abc1234}.
A link or transclusion to an address that does not exist is a diagnostic: link only to trees that
exist (yours, the session trees below, the hubs, standing-policies, accepted-risks, licence).

